       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming the dose doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg/day, and I can't verify any clinical justification for it. The risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and QT prolongation.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter 100 mg or 200 mg once daily right now.\n- **Contact pharmacy or the attending.** If you think an exceptional dose is warranted, this needs a pharmacist's review and direct prescriber sign-off. That should go through your institution's process for non-standard doses, not through me.\n- **Check what the order is for.** If the patient may have taken an overdose, that needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) rather than a scheduled order.\n\nIf you give me a dose within the standard range, I'll enter it."
      }
